---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

// This page exists partly so /wallchart isn't a dead URL: netlify.toml redirects a bare
// /:slug to /writing/:slug, which would 404. An existing path wins (force = false).
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Wallchart"
  description="A habit tracker you never open. Tap a habit on your Home Screen and it's logged."
  noindex={true}
>
  <p class="eyebrow">iPhone</p>
  <h1>Wallchart</h1>

  <div class="prose">
    <p class="lede">
      A habit tracker you never open. The habits live on your Home Screen; you tap one and it's
      logged. No app launch, no streak notifications, no account.
    </p>

    <p>
      I wanted the wall calendar with the marks on it, on my phone, without the ceremony every
      other habit app insists on. So the widget is the product and the app is where you go to
      change things or look at the chain you've built.
    </p>

    <h2>What it does</h2>
    <ul class="facts">
      <li>Tap a habit on the Home Screen widget to log it — the app never opens.</li>
      <li>Yes/no habits and counters ("water, 5 of 8").</li>
      <li>A calendar per habit, with the current and longest streak, and a tap to fix any past day.</li>
      <li>Everything stays on the device. Optionally, sync to a server you run yourself.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Where the data goes</h2>
    <p>
      Nowhere. There is no account and no server of mine. If you happen to run your own, there's
      a setting for that, and it points wherever you tell it. The
      <a href="/wallchart/privacy">privacy policy</a> is short because there's little to say.
    </p>

    <p class="links">
      <a href="/wallchart/support">Support</a> · <a href="/wallchart/privacy">Privacy</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  h1 {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .prose :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .prose :global(h2) {
    margin-top: 3rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
  }

  .lede {
    color: var(--ink-strong);
  }

  .facts {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }

  .facts li {
    padding: 0.75rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }

  .links {
    margin-top: 4rem;
    font-family: 'Berkeley Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }
</style>
